local _, ns = ...
local E = ns.DB.entries
E["npc:brann-bronzebeard"] = {t="npc",n="Brann Bronzebeard",z="silithus",s="Brann Bronzebeard is the youngest brother of King Magni and the late Muradin, renowned throughout Azeroth as a peerless explorer, archaeologist, and founding leader of the Explorers' League. Driven by an insatiable curiosity for titan ruins and ancient history, his wanderlust has led him deep into the deadly wastes of Silithus. He has recently vanished past the impenetrable Scarab Wall, leaving his field companions behind with only baffling clues and his beloved pet ape.",h="Brann Bronzebeard is the youngest brother of King Magni and the late Muradin, renowned throughout Azeroth as...",sec={{t="A Royal Wanderer",b="While his eldest brother Magni rules Ironforge from the throne and Muradin served on battlefield frontlines, Brann took to the open wilds. He was a veteran warrior of the Second War, fighting in the Siege of Ironforge and following High General Anduin Lothar and Turalyon all the way to the Dark Portal's destruction. Yet peacetime turned his formidable constitution toward uncovering the forgotten past. As a leader of the Explorers' League, Brann charted vast swathes of the Eastern Kingdoms—from Elwynn Forest to the untamed jungles of Zul'Gurub—before turning his gaze across the Great Sea to the mysteries of ancient Kalimdor.",sp=0},{t="Trouble in Silithus",b="Drawn south by reports from the Cenarion Circle concerning the Old God C'Thun and the slumbering qiraji swarm, Brann established the Bronzebeard Encampment in southern Silithus alongside fellow explorers Rutgar Glyphshaper and Frankal Stonebridge. Tragedy struck when the priestess Natalia Mar'alith, maddened by the whispering horrors of the shifting sands, raided their camp. Natalia ambushed Brann and knocked him senseless before his pet ape, Glibb, flew into a defensive fury and drove her screeching toward Hive'Regal.",sp=1},{t="Beyond the Scarab Wall",b="Rather than retreating after the terrifying assault, the intrepid archaeologist became obsessed with entering the sealed kingdom behind the Scarab Wall. Brann discovered a hidden subterranean tunnel that bypassed the ancient barrier entirely and ventured inside alone, leaving Glibb in the care of his expedition with strict written orders to provide the ape with plenty of food, water, and affectionate hugs. His companions remain stranded in southern Silithus, desperately awaiting word from within the silithid hives.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Brann Bronzebeard?",a="He is the youngest brother of King Magni Bronzebeard of Ironforge and a co-founder and driving force behind the dwarven Explorers' League. Rather than sitting in council chambers, Brann is a legendary archaeologist and cartographer who travels Azeroth's most dangerous frontiers to uncover titan artifacts and lost civilizations.",al={"who is brann","brann lore","brann bronzebeard backstory"}},{q="Where is Brann Bronzebeard right now?",a="He has slipped through an underground fissure into Ahn'Qiraj past the sealed Scarab Wall in southern Silithus. His associates, Rutgar Glyphshaper and Frankal Stonebridge, still tend the Bronzebeard Encampment along the southern cliffs, hoping he emerges alive.",al={"brann location","where to find brann","where is brann in silithus"}},{q="What happened to his camp in Silithus?",a="The encampment was ambushed by the maddened night elf priestess Natalia Mar'alith. She struck Brann unconscious, but his pet ape Glibb flew into a defensive rage and fought her off, chasing her into the nearby insectoid tunnels of Hive'Regal.",al={"what happened at bronzebeard encampment","who attacked brann's camp","natalia attack brann"}},{q="Who is Glibb?",a="Glibb is Brann Bronzebeard's companion ape. Glibb saved Brann's life during the surprise attack by Natalia Mar'alith. When Brann departed into the tunnels beneath Ahn'Qiraj, he left Glibb behind at Bronzebeard Encampment with urgent orders for his crew to keep the beast well-fed and hugged.",al={"glibb ape","brann's monkey","brann pet"}},{q="Did Brann fight in the Second War?",a="Yes. Brann fought in the Siege of Ironforge before marching alongside his brother Muradin under Anduin Lothar and Turalyon to Blackrock Mountain, fighting forest trolls and orcs all the way to the Dark Portal.",al={"brann second war","was brann in the alliance army","brann and muradin war"}},{q="Why is Brann interested in Silithus?",a="Brann was drawn to the desert by Cenarion Circle whispers concerning the Old God C'Thun, titan history, and the trapped qiraji empire, prompting him to find a way beyond the sealed Scarab Wall to inspect the ruins first-hand.",al={"why did brann go to silithus","brann silithus purpose","brann c'thun"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As the youngest brother of King Magni, Brann embodies the dwarven passion for digging into the roots of their titan heritage.",["faction:Alliance"]="Brann's expeditionary work directly fuels the knowledge and archives of the Alliance, though his habit of vanishing without a trace often drives Ironforge's leadership to distraction."},kw={"ahn'qiraj","brann","bronzebeard","explorers league","frankal","glibb","natalia mar'alith","rutgar","scarab wall","silithus"},rel={"subzone:bronzebeard-encampment","subzone:scarab-wall","npc:rutgar-glyphshaper","npc:natalia-mar-alith","subzone:hive-regal","topic:explorers-league","zone:silithus","zone:ironforge"},src={"Brann Bronzebeard"}}
E["npc:commander-mar-alith"] = {t="npc",n="Commander Mar'alith",z="silithus",s="Commander Mar'alith is the stalwart night elf military commander directing the Cenarion Circle's vanguard at Cenarion Hold in Silithus. Clad in heavy armor and wielding a grand glaive, he coordinates the martial resistance against the silithid swarms and Twilight's Hammer cultists. Beneath his resolute leadership lies a deep personal sorrow regarding the mysterious fate of his beloved wife, Natalia.",h="Commander Mar'alith is the stalwart night elf military commander directing the Cenarion Circle's vanguard at...",sec={{t="Commander of the Hold",b="Stationed at the heart of Cenarion Hold, Commander Mar'alith bears the tremendous responsibility of safeguarding the Circle's desert bastion. While the druids unravel the ancient ecological and cosmic anomalies of Silithus, Mar'alith handles the grim, practical necessities of war. He oversees tactical strikes against the bustling silithid hives of Hive'Ashi, Hive'Zora, and Hive'Regal, ensuring that the relentless insectoid incursions do not overwhelm the expedition's central foothold.",sp=0},{t="Grief in the Desert",b="Despite his stern military bearing, Mar'alith is visibly strained by a harrowing personal tragedy. His beloved wife, Natalia Mar'alith, ventured into the shifting sands on an assignment for the Circle and failed to return. Caught between his duty to the Cenarion expedition and agonizing grief, the commander appears increasingly distracted, clinging to whatever hope remains while desperate for news of what truly became of her in the wastes.",sp=0},{t="A Tragic Fate",b="The dreadful truth of Natalia's disappearance weighs heavily on the commander. Those who trace her footsteps discover that she succumbed to madness amidst the whispers of the desert and was brainwashed by a Qiraji crystal into the service of C'Thun. Learning of her tragic end leaves Mar'alith deeply shaken, forcing the commander to endure devastating heartbreak while continuing to direct the defense of Silithus against the looming horrors underground.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Commander Mar'alith?",a="Commander Mar'alith is a night elf officer serving as the supreme military commander of the Cenarion Circle's forces at Cenarion Hold. He organizes scouts, defense forces, and tactical strikes against the silithid hives across Silithus.",al={"maralith","who is commander maralith","night elf commander silithus"}},{q="Where can Commander Mar'alith be found?",a="He is located inside Cenarion Hold, the primary neutral settlement established by the Cenarion Circle in the windswept sands of Silithus.",al={"maralith location","where is maralith"}},{q="What happened to his wife, Natalia?",a="Natalia Mar'alith vanished into the desert during an expedition and never returned. Adventurers who follow her trail through Silithus can learn what became of her.",al={"where is natalia","dearest natalia","natalia maralith fate"},sp=1},{q="Why does Mar'alith seem absent-minded?",a="The commander is wracked with sorrow and anxiety over the absence and fate of his missing wife, which frequently distracts him even as he struggles to direct the defense of the fortress.",al={"why is maralith distracted","maralith acting weird"}},{q="What tasks does Commander Mar'alith assign to adventurers?",a="Mar'alith issues combat assignments directing champions to cull silithid forces in Hive'Ashi, Hive'Zora, and Hive'Regal, counter the Twilight's Hammer, and investigate the fate of his missing wife.",al={"maralith quests","what quests does maralith give"}},{q="Is Commander Mar'alith a druid?",a="No. Although he serves the Cenarion Circle, Mar'alith is an armored sentinel and warrior commander who oversees the expedition's martial defense and tactical operations rather than wielding druidic magic.",al={"is maralith a druid","maralith class"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Mar'alith exemplifies the dedication of Kaldorei sentinels and warriors who stand guard alongside the druidic order, defending Kalimdor against ancient threats despite steep personal sacrifice.",["class:Warrior"]="Clad in heavy plate and brandishing a massive glaive, Mar'alith directs raw battlefield warfare amidst a settlement primarily populated by mystics and nature keepers."},kw={"cenarion circle","cenarion hold","commander mar'alith","hive'ashi","hive'regal","hive'zora","mar'alith","natalia mar'alith","silithus"},rel={"subzone:cenarion-hold","npc:natalia-mar-alith","zone:silithus","topic:cenarion-circle","subzone:hive-ashi","subzone:hive-zora","subzone:hive-regal","topic:night-elf"},src={"Commander Mar'alith"}}
E["npc:highlord-demitrian"] = {t="npc",n="Highlord Demitrian",z="silithus",s="Highlord Demitrian is a solitary human hermit dwelling amidst the strange crystals of northwestern Silithus. Describing himself as a loyal servant of Prince Thunderaan, he possesses the esoteric knowledge required to wake the slumbering elemental lord. Adventurers bearing ancient elemental bindings seek him out to unlock the power of the Windseeker.",h="Highlord Demitrian is a solitary human hermit dwelling amidst the strange crystals of northwestern Silithus.",sec={{t="Hermit of the Crystal Vale",b="Found lingering at an abandoned encampment in the Crystal Vale, Demitrian appears out of place in the desolate wastes of Silithus. Though he is tied to the Twilight's Hammer whose ravaged camp he haunts, Demitrian acts above all as a herald for Prince Thunderaan, the Windseeker. He treats visitors with aloof indifference unless they carry proof of the Windseeker's shattered essence.",sp=0},{t="The Vessel of Rebirth",b="Demitrian's purpose is tied entirely to Thunderaan's resurrection. Should an adventurer present him with the Bindings of the Windseeker—relics torn from fire elementals within the Molten Core—Demitrian provides the Vessel of Rebirth. He demands rare elemental reagents, including vast quantities of enchanted elementium and the essence of the Firelord, to reconstitute his prince's physical form.",sp=1},{t="Betrayal of the Windseeker",b="Demitrian's devotion is repaid swiftly with treachery. Upon gathering the required components and summoning Thunderaan forth into the Crystal Vale, the Windseeker attacks rather than rewards his mortal servant. Once adventurers vanquish the furious elemental lord, Demitrian cowers in terror, surrendering the Dormant Wind Kissed Blade from which the legendary sword Thunderfury is forged.",sp=2}},faq={{q="Where can I find Highlord Demitrian?",a="He is located in the far northwestern corner of Silithus, standing near the Ravaged Twilight Camp inside the Crystal Vale.",al={"demitrian location","where is demitrian","demitrian silithus spot"}},{q="Why does Demitrian only give a generic response?",a="Demitrian will not offer his legendary quest chain unless you are carrying at least one half of the Bindings of the Windseeker, which are rare treasures held by Baron Geddon and Garr in the Molten Core.",al={"demitrian won't talk to me","how to get demitrian quest","demitrian gossip"}},{q="What is Demitrian's relationship to Prince Thunderaan?",a="Demitrian is the sworn mortal servant of Prince Thunderaan. He has dedicated himself to finding the prince's severed bindings and restoring the elemental lord to the physical plane.",al={"who does demitrian serve","demitrian thunderaan connection","is demitrian twilight hammer"}},{q="What happens when you bring him all the materials for the vessel?",a="Demitrian conducts a ritual that unleashes Prince Thunderaan in the Crystal Vale. Thunderaan immediately turns hostile, requiring a raid group to strike down the restored Windseeker.",al={"summoning thunderaan","what does demitrian do with the vessel","crystal vale summon"},sp=1},{q="Is Demitrian affiliated with the Twilight's Hammer cult?",a="He is tied to the Twilight's Hammer and dwells in their ravaged camp, and he speaks of the Old Gods with reverence. Still, his sworn devotion is to his master, Prince Thunderaan.",al={"is demitrian a cultist","demitrian twilight camp","demitrian faction"}},{q="How do you get Thunderfury from him?",a="After Thunderaan is summoned and defeated, Demitrian is left cowering on the ground. Speaking to him allows you to claim the Dormant Wind Kissed Blade, which can be formed into Thunderfury, Blessed Blade of the Windseeker.",al={"how to get thunderfury","thunderfury quest finish","demitrian blade"},sp=1}},ang={["profession:Blacksmithing"]="Demitrian's demands for Thunderaan's rebirth require extensive blacksmithing mastery to forge Enchanted Elementium Bars from raw ore and fiery essences.",["class:Warrior"]="Warriors seeking the legendary blade Thunderfury must seek out Demitrian to initiate the trial of unbinding and awakening the Windseeker.",["class:Rogue"]="Rogues hunting the legendary blade of the Windseeker must bargain with Demitrian in Silithus to restore the shattered prince."},kw={"crystal vale","demitrian","highlord demitrian","silithus","thunderaan","thunderfury","vessel of rebirth","windseeker"},rel={"npc:thunderaan","subzone:crystal-vale","zone:silithus","subzone:ravaged-twilight-camp","topic:elemental-plane","topic:skywall"},src={"Highlord Demitrian"}}
E["npc:natalia-mar-alith"] = {t="npc",n="Natalia Mar'alith",z="silithus",s="Mistress Natalia Mar'alith is a night elf priestess and Cenarion Circle researcher who went missing deep within the silithid nests of Hive'Regal. She ventured into the wastes of Silithus alongside her husband, Commander Mar'alith, before departing on an expedition into the hives.",h="Mistress Natalia Mar'alith is a night elf priestess and Cenarion Circle researcher who went missing deep...",sec={{t="A Tragic Descent",b="When the Cenarion Circle established their outpost at Cenarion Hold to monitor the awakening sands, Natalia accompanied her husband, Commander Mar'alith, into the wastes. Eager to unravel the mystery behind the resurgence of the silithid and the ancient Qiraji ruins, she joined an exploratory party led by the famed explorer Brann Bronzebeard, accompanied by the dwarven researchers Rutgar Glyphshaper and Frankal Stonebridge.",sp=0},{t="The Crystal of Hive'Regal",b="The expedition tracked strange emanations into the southern reaches of Hive'Regal. Deep in the hive's heart, they uncovered a colossal crystal etched with ancient Qiraji glyphs. Drawn by its whispering resonance, Natalia leaned in to study the markings closely. The dark magic within overwhelmed her mind in moments, fracturing her sanity and binding her will to C'Thun. Her dwarven companions carried her out to Cenarion Hold, where the druids woke her, but weeks later she stormed back into their camp, possessed and demanding a return to the hive, and had to be fought off. She is now a zealous guardian of the hive's dread master.",sp=1},{t="The Commander's Anguish",b="Back at Cenarion Hold, Commander Mar'alith clings desperately to the hope that his wife can be saved, refusing to accept that her mind has been irrevocably shattered. Yet anyone who braves Hive'Regal finds not a captive in need of rescue, but a ruthless servant of madness wielding sacred priest magic warped by the Old God's malice.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Natalia Mar'alith?",a="Natalia Mar'alith is a night elf priestess of the Cenarion Circle and the wife of Commander Mar'alith. She joined Brann Bronzebeard's scouting expedition into Hive'Regal to study the resurgence of the silithid, where she fell victim to dark ancient magic.",al={"natalia maralith","who is natalia","commander maraliths wife"},sp=1},{q="Where can I find Natalia Mar'alith?",a="She is located deep within the insectoid tunnels of Hive'Regal in southern Silithus, standing vigil before a glowing glyph-covered crystal.",al={"natalia location","where is natalia","hive regal priestess"}},{q="Why is Natalia hostile to adventurers?",a="While examining a Qiraji crystal, Natalia was utterly corrupted and mentally broken by the whisperings of the Old God C'Thun. She now fanatically defends the crystal from anyone who enters the hive.",al={"why did natalia attack me","why is natalia crazy","natalia brainwashed"},sp=1},{q="Who was with Natalia when she went missing?",a="She ventured into Hive'Regal with Brann Bronzebeard, Rutgar Glyphshaper, and Frankal Stonebridge. Rutgar and Frankal survived the ordeal and retreated to the Bronzebeard Encampment in southern Silithus to tell the tale.",al={"natalia expedition","who was with natalia","brann and natalia"}},{q="Why is she so dangerous in combat?",a="Natalia retains her formidable priest powers, continually scattering attackers with Psychic Scream and restoring her strength through near-costless Greater Heals, making her very difficult to overcome without constant interruptions.",al={"natalia fight","how to beat natalia","natalia heal"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Natalia's tragic fall is a somber reminder to the kaldorei that even their most dedicated priestesses are vulnerable to the ancient horrors buried beneath the sands of Silithus.",["faction:Alliance"]="Rutgar Glyphshaper and Frankal Stonebridge at the Bronzebeard Encampment share the grim details of her fall with Alliance explorers retracing Brann's expedition."},kw={"brann bronzebeard","cenarion hold","hive'regal","into the maw of madness","mar'alith","maralith","natalia","silithus"},rel={"npc:commander-mar-alith","subzone:hive-regal","zone:silithus","subzone:bronzebeard-encampment","npc:brann-bronzebeard","npc:rutgar-glyphshaper","topic:cenarion-circle","topic:old-god"},src={"Natalia Mar'alith"}}
E["npc:rutgar-glyphshaper"] = {t="npc",n="Rutgar Glyphshaper",z="silithus",s="Rutgar Glyphshaper is a dwarven archaeologist stationed at the Bronzebeard Encampment in the southern reaches of Silithus. As a member of Brann Bronzebeard's expedition, he studies ancient silithid relics and runes, striving to uncover the mystery of the hives even after Brann wanders off into the desert.",h="Rutgar Glyphshaper is a dwarven archaeologist stationed at the Bronzebeard Encampment in the southern reaches...",sec={{t="The Bronzebeard Expedition",b="Rutgar Glyphshaper traveled to Silithus under the leadership of Brann Bronzebeard to investigate the vast silithid hives and unearth lost relics buried beneath the desert wastes. Establishing their base at the Bronzebeard Encampment south of Cenarion Hold, Rutgar and his companions frequently ventured directly into the bug hives to harvest inscribed stones and runic artifacts, often cooperating with Cenarion night elf researchers.",sp=0},{t="Trouble in the Hives",b="During an expedition into Hive'Regal alongside the night elf priestess Natalia Mar'alith, the party discovered a strange glyphed crystal. The relic exerted a trance-like hold over Natalia, forcing the dwarves to carry her out and deliver her to Cenarion Hold for healing. When she later returned to the dwarven camp in a wild frenzy demanding to return to the hive, Rutgar and the expedition were forced to fight her off in a desperate brawl before she fled back into the dunes.",sp=1},{t="Deciphering the Silithid",b="With Brann Bronzebeard mysteriously disappearing into the wastes as he is prone to do, Rutgar remains at camp to continue their scholarship. He focuses on gathering crystalline rubbings and deciphering the insectoid glyphs scattered across the silithid hives, trying to piece together the history of the hives and trace where Brann might have vanished.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Rutgar Glyphshaper?",a="He is an explorer and scholar who accompanied Brann Bronzebeard on an archaeological expedition to Silithus, currently based at the Bronzebeard Encampment.",al={"rutgar","who is rutgar","rutgar glyphshaper info"}},{q="Where is Brann Bronzebeard?",a="Brann wandered off alone into the wastes of Silithus on one of his typical solo scouting trips, leaving Rutgar and the rest of the crew to maintain the encampment and research the hives.",al={"where is brann","where did brann go","brann missing"}},{q="What happened to Natalia Mar'alith at the camp?",a="After falling under the influence of an ancient crystal in Hive'Regal, Natalia Mar'alith returned to the Bronzebeard Encampment in a violent rage, attacking Rutgar, Brann, and the crew before vanishing back into the desert.",al={"what happened to natalia","natalia attack","priestess attacked camp"},sp=1},{q="Why is Rutgar studying the silithid crystals?",a="Rutgar is attempting to translate the ancient glyphs carved into the crystals within the hives, seeking to understand the silithid's origins and find clues regarding Brann's whereabouts.",al={"why glyphs","what is rutgar studying","glyphed crystals"}},{q="Has Ironforge sent aid to the expedition?",a="No. The expedition requested military support from Ironforge, but the dwarven kingdom declined, claiming its forces are already stretched too thin defending the realm.",al={"ironforge reinforcements","ironforge army silithus"}},{q="Where is the Bronzebeard Encampment located?",a="It is located in southern Silithus, situated in the desert sands south of Cenarion Hold and just west of Hive'Regal.",al={"where is bronzebeard encampment","encampment location"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Dwarves will recognize Rutgar's stubborn dedication to the Explorer's League, risking life and limb deep in hostile insect hives for the sake of ancient knowledge.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance adventurers find a rare outpost of friendly faces in the harsh southern desert, though Rutgar's crew receives no official backing from the Ironforge crown."},kw={"brann","bronzebeard","crystal","glyphs","glyphshaper","maralith","regal","rutgar","silithus"},rel={"subzone:bronzebeard-encampment","npc:brann-bronzebeard","subzone:hive-regal","subzone:cenarion-hold","zone:silithus","zone:ironforge","topic:dwarf"},src={"Rutgar Glyphshaper"}}
E["npc:thunderaan"] = {t="npc",n="Thunderaan",z="silithus",s="Prince Thunderaan is the ancient Prince of Air, a colossal elemental struck down and betrayed during the ancient wars between fire and wind. Consumed in part by Ragnaros the Firelord, his remnant essence was sealed into shattered bindings entrusted to the Firelord's lieutenants. Adventurers who recover these relics can seek out Highlord Demitrian in Silithus to unleash him once more.",h="Prince Thunderaan is the ancient Prince of Air, a colossal elemental struck down and betrayed during the...",sec={{t="The Elemental Sundering",b="Long ago, during the Elemental Sundering—a five-thousand-year clash fought between the forces of fire and air deep within Azeroth—Ragnaros sought to destroy and consume Thunderaan. The Prince was ambushed and betrayed by Ragnaros's powerful lieutenants, Baron Geddon and Garr, before being struck down by the Firelord's hammer, Sulfuras. Although defeated, Thunderaan's essence proved too mighty for Ragnaros to fully absorb.",sp=0},{t="The Shattered Talisman",b="Unable to entirely devour the Prince of Air, Ragnaros sealed what little remained of Thunderaan's essence inside a talisman of elemental binding. To prevent the Prince from ever reforming, the Firelord shattered the talisman into two flawless halves. He entrusted one piece to Baron Geddon and the other to Garr, hiding both within the volcanic depths of the Molten Core beneath Blackrock Mountain.",sp=0},{t="Rebirth in Silithus",b="Those daring enough to invade the Molten Core can wrench both halves of the binding from Ragnaros's lieutenants. Presenting these fragments to Highlord Demitrian, an eccentric hermit allied with the Twilight's Hammer in the arid dunes of Silithus, initiates a ritual to manifest the Prince of Air. Yet the newborn elemental arises not in gratitude, but in raw, cyclonic fury, forcing summoners to strike him down to claim his legendary blade, Thunderfury, Blessed Blade of the Windseeker.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Thunderaan?",a="Thunderaan is the Prince of Air, a noble and devastating elemental lord aligned with the wind. Long ago, he was overwhelmed by Ragnaros the Firelord and sealed away in an elemental prison.",al={"who is prince thunderaan","prince of air","thunderaan lore"}},{q="How was Thunderaan defeated originally?",a="During the Elemental Sundering, Ragnaros conspired with his lieutenants Baron Geddon and Garr to betray the Prince. Thunderaan was crushed by Sulfuras, and while Ragnaros feasted on his essence, he could not digest it entirely, forcing him to lock the remainder inside a split talisman.",al={"how did thunderaan die","ragnaros vs thunderaan","elemental sundering"}},{q="Where are the pieces of his binding held?",a="The two flawless halves of Thunderaan's binding are held by Garr and Baron Geddon, deep inside the Molten Core under Blackrock Mountain.",al={"where are bindings of the windseeker","bindings of thunderaan location","garr and geddon bindings"}},{q="Why is Highlord Demitrian in Silithus involved?",a="Highlord Demitrian is a disciple of the Twilight's Hammer residing in Silithus who possesses the arcane and elemental knowledge needed to reconstitute the shattered talisman and summon the Prince of Air into Azeroth.",al={"who is demitrian","highlord demitrian thunderaan","how to summon thunderaan"}},{q="What happens when Thunderaan is summoned in Silithus?",a="Rather than being peacefully freed or offering thanks, Thunderaan manifests as a raging elemental tempest. Adventurers must band together to defeat his whirlwind strikes and lightning attacks in order to extract his blade.",al={"thunderaan fight","what happens after summoning"},sp=1},{q="What weapon is tied to Thunderaan?",a="Defeating Thunderaan allows a champion to claim Thunderfury, Blessed Blade of the Windseeker, an ancient, storm-infused blade housing the core of the Prince's tempestuous might.",al={"thunderfury","windseeker sword","thunderaan sword"},sp=1}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As spiritual custodians of the elements, shaman recognize Thunderaan as one of the purest and most wrathful embodiments of air and lightning on Azeroth.",["class:Warrior"]="Warriors revere the legend of Thunderaan because conquering him yields Thunderfury, Blessed Blade of the Windseeker, one of the most formidable one-handed weapons ever forged.",["class:Rogue"]="Rogues with a taste for unmatched speed and lightning-quick combat covet the Prince of Air's fallen essence, bound within the iconic blade Thunderfury."},kw={"bindings","demitrian","garr","geddon","molten core","prince of air","ragnaros","silithus","thunderaan","thunderfury","windseeker"},rel={"npc:highlord-demitrian","zone:silithus","subzone:blackrock-mountain","topic:twilight-s-hammer","topic:skywall"},src={"Thunderaan"}}
E["subzone:bones-of-grakkarond"] = {t="subzone",n="Bones of Grakkarond",z="silithus",s="The Bones of Grakkarond are the skeletal remains of a massive bronze dragon lying bleached under the sun of central Silithus. Slain during the ancient War of the Shifting Sands, this fallen wyrm serves as a grim monument held sacred by the qiraji's Anubisath sentinels.",h="The Bones of Grakkarond are the skeletal remains of a massive bronze dragon lying bleached under the sun of...",sec={{t="A Monument of the Shifting Sands",b="Sprawled across the windswept dunes of central Silithus lies the colossal ribcage and skull of Grakkarond, a bronze dragon who met his demise during the ancient War of the Shifting Sands. In that apocalyptic clash a millennium ago, the great dragon was struck down by Ossirian the Unscarred, an Anubisath warrior elevated by the dark powers of the city-kingdom. To the Anubisath, this battlefield trophy is a sacred testament to their might over the dragonflights, left untouched where he fell.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Whose bones are these?",a="These are the remains of Grakkarond, a great bronze dragon of the Bronze Dragonflight. He fell in battle against the insectoid forces of Ahn'Qiraj a thousand years ago during the War of the Shifting Sands.",al={"who was grakkarond","what dragon died here","dragon skeleton silithus"}},{q="Who killed Grakkarond?",a="Grakkarond was slain by the Anubisath warrior Ossirian the Unscarred. Ossirian's triumph over the bronze wyrm earned him immense renown and dark blessings from the masters of Ahn'Qiraj.",al={"who killed the dragon","how did grakkarond die"}},{q="Why do the Anubisath revere this place?",a="The Anubisath consider the skeleton sacred because it commemorates their decisive victory over a mighty dragonflight. It stands in the open dunes as a triumphant symbol of their strength against those who came to seal them away.",al={"why are the bones sacred","anubisath bones"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The skeleton serves as a stark reminder of the War of the Shifting Sands, where kaldorei and the four dragonflights fought side-by-side to push back the qiraji onslaught."},kw={"anubisath","bones of grakkarond","bronze dragon","grakkarond","ossirian the unscarred","silithus","war of the shifting sands"},rel={"zone:silithus"},src={"Bones of Grakkarond"}}
E["subzone:bronzebeard-encampment"] = {t="subzone",n="Bronzebeard Encampment",z="silithus",s="Bronzebeard Encampment is a rugged dwarven outpost perched in southern Silithus, just east of the massive Scarab Wall. Staffed by hardy explorers and researchers from the Explorer's League, the camp serves as an operational base for investigating ancient silithid glyphs and the lingering mysteries buried beneath the desert sands.",h="Bronzebeard Encampment is a rugged dwarven outpost perched in southern Silithus, just east of the massive...",sec={{t="A Foothold in the Shifting Sands",b="Positioned against the desolate southern bluffs of Silithus, Bronzebeard Encampment offers a rare refuge of dwarven grit in an otherwise hostile wasteland. Founded under the auspices of Ironforge's archaeological pursuits, the camp sits within sight of the towering Scarab Wall. Here, researchers like Rutgar Glyphshaper and Frankal Stonebridge braved scorching heat, scorpids, and encroaching silithid swarms to study the peculiar inscriptions and monuments left behind by forgotten civilizations.",sp=0},{t="Glyphs and Desperation",b="Life in the encampment is far from a quiet dig. With the silithid menace spreading out of subterranean hives across the wastes and dangerous horrors like the monstrous scorpid Deathclasp prowling nearby sands, the outpost balances rigorous scholarship with sheer survival. The researchers rely heavily on visiting adventurers to retrieve rubbings of obscure glyphs, decipher ancient insectoid tongues, and search for lost companions who ventured too deep into the madness of the desert.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Bronzebeard Encampment located?",a="The encampment is located in southern Silithus, situated east of the colossal Scarab Wall and north of the southern mountain ridge.",al={"where is bronzebeard encampment","bronzebeard camp location","how to find bronzebeard encampment"}},{q="Who runs the Bronzebeard Encampment?",a="The camp is staffed by members and associates of the dwarven Explorer's League, including the glyph researcher Rutgar Glyphshaper, Frankal Stonebridge, and their companion Glibb.",al={"who is at bronzebeard encampment","bronzebeard camp npcs","who leads bronzebeard camp"}},{q="What are the dwarves studying here?",a="The researchers are dedicated to deciphering ancient stone glyphs, understanding the silithid communication system, and unearthing the long-buried secrets of southern Kalimdor.",al={"why are dwarves in silithus","what is rutgar studying","purpose of bronzebeard encampment"}},{q="What threats lurk near the encampment?",a="The surrounding desert is prowled by aggressive silithid bugs, sand scorpions, and the notorious giant scorpid known as Deathclasp, Terror of the Sands, which nests just to the southeast.",al={"dangers near bronzebeard camp","deathclasp location","bronzebeard camp monsters"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="The outpost showcases the unwavering tenacity of the Explorer's League, proving that no barren desert is too hostile for Ironforge dwarves seeking historical truth.",["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance travelers navigating the grim expanse of Silithus, this remote camp provides a welcome friendly outpost far south of Cenarion Hold."},kw={"bronzebeard encampment","deathclasp","explorers league","frankal stonebridge","glibb","rutgar glyphshaper","scarab wall","silithus"},rel={"zone:silithus","subzone:scarab-wall","npc:rutgar-glyphshaper"},src={"Bronzebeard Encampment"}}
E["subzone:cenarion-hold"] = {t="subzone",n="Cenarion Hold",z="silithus",s="Cenarion Hold is the fortified stronghold of the Cenarion Circle situated in the harsh desert of Silithus. Established to keep watch over ancient dangers buried beneath the sands, it stands as one of the largest druidic settlements on Kalimdor and a rare safe haven in an unforgiving wasteland.",h="Cenarion Hold is the fortified stronghold of the Cenarion Circle situated in the harsh desert of Silithus.",sec={{t="A Bastion in the Dunes",b="Perched among the desolate sands of Silithus, Cenarion Hold serves as the southern command hub for the Cenarion Circle. Reached by winding past Un'Goro Crater, the fortress was raised to monitor the dormant threats sealed beneath the desert after the historic War of the Shifting Sands. In an inhospitable expanse teeming with insectoid silithid and arid storms, the stronghold provides vital shelter, trade, and logistical support for night elf and tauren druids alike who stand sentinel over the imprisoned horrors of the past.",sp=0},{t="Neutral Ground",b="Because the duty of safeguarding the world from ancient evils transcends mortal squabbles, Cenarion Hold operates under strict Cenarion Circle neutrality. Both Alliance and Horde travelers are admitted inside its walls, welcomed by local quartermasters and wardens whose supply lines remain precarious. With flight routes connecting it back to outposts in Feralas, Tanaris, and Un'Goro Crater, the hold acts as the lone staging ground for mortal adventurers brave enough to investigate the rising unrest in the desert.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who controls Cenarion Hold?",a="The stronghold is governed and garrisoned entirely by the Cenarion Circle, the druidic order founded by Malfurion Stormrage. It maintains complete neutrality, welcoming members of both the Alliance and the Horde.",al={"who runs cenarion hold","cenarion hold faction","is cenarion hold neutral"}},{q="Why was the fortress built out here in the desert?",a="It was established following the War of the Shifting Sands to stand watch over the imprisoned Old God buried deep beneath Silithus and to suppress the resurgence of the insectoid silithid swarming the region.",al={"why is cenarion hold in silithus","purpose of cenarion hold","why did druids build here"}},{q="How do you travel to Cenarion Hold?",a="Travelers on foot typically take the steep mountain path leading northwest from the Mossy Pile in Un'Goro Crater. Flight networks also link the hold to flight masters in Gadgetzan, Un'Goro, and Feralas.",al={"how to get to cenarion hold","cenarion hold path","getting into silithus"}},{q="Can members of both factions use services here?",a="Yes. The merchants and flight handlers inside Cenarion Hold trade freely with any adventurer willing to brave the desert, regardless of political allegiances.",al={"is it safe for horde","can alliance rest here","cenarion hold vendors"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As one of the largest druidic enclaves outside of Moonglade, Cenarion Hold embodies the Circle's pledge to preserve natural balance against cosmic horrors.",["race:NightElf"]="For the night elves, this fortress honors ancient sacrifices made during the catastrophic War of the Shifting Sands millennia ago."},kw={"cenarion circle","cenarion hold","druids","kalimdor","shifting sands","silithid","silithus"},rel={"topic:cenarion-circle","zone:silithus","quest:5921","zone:ungoro","zone:feralas","subzone:gadgetzan","topic:old-god"},src={"Cenarion Hold"}}
E["subzone:crystal-vale"] = {t="subzone",n="Crystal Vale",z="silithus",s="Tucked away in the far northwestern corner of Silithus, the Crystal Vale is a remote canyon dominated by jagged mineral spires and swirling elemental forces. Earth and air elementals roam its rocky flats, guarding rich veins of raw ore. It is also a site of potent summoning magic, deeply tied to the ancient elemental lords.",h="Tucked away in the far northwestern corner of Silithus, the Crystal Vale is a remote canyon dominated by...",sec={{t="A Confluence of Stone and Wind",b="The Crystal Vale stands distinct from the barren desert sands of southern Silithus. Framed by steep cliffs, the basin is filled with shimmering crystalloid formations, roaming earthen elementals, and roaring whirlwinds of living air. Rich deposits of thorium draw occasional daring prospectors, but the vale is far from quiet. The elemental beings here are inherently hostile to intruders, guarding a realm that feels steeped in the primal conflicts of primordial Azeroth.",sp=0},{t="The Slumber of the Windseeker",b="Beyond its minerals and native spirits, the Crystal Vale holds deep significance for ancient elemental powers. It is here that Highlord Demitrian lingers, harboring the secrets of Prince Thunderaan, the Windseeker. Those who gather the severed elemental bindings of the fallen prince and the rarest forged metals are directed to this valley, where the imprisoned lord of air can be coaxed from his bindings and challenged in open battle.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is the Crystal Vale located?",a="The Crystal Vale is situated in the far northwestern reaches of Silithus, nestled against the mountainous rim that borders the desert.",al={"where is crystal vale","crystal vale map","crystal vale location"}},{q="What creatures inhabit this valley?",a="The canyon is primarily populated by aggressive air and earth elementals that drift and stomp around the mineral outcrops.",al={"crystal vale mobs","what lives in crystal vale","elementals in crystal vale"}},{q="Who is Highlord Demitrian and why is he here?",a="Highlord Demitrian is a solitary hermit dwelling in the vale who holds profound knowledge of Prince Thunderaan. He aids champions capable of reuniting the Windseeker's bindings to summon the elemental prince.",al={"who is demitrian","highlord demitrian crystal vale","demitrian location"}},{q="What is the Ravaged Twilight Camp?",a="It is the wreckage of a Twilight's Hammer encampment within the vale, overrun and shattered by the violent elemental denizens that claim the canyon.",al={"ravaged twilight camp crystal vale","twilight camp in vale","destroyed twilight camp"}}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="The craggy edges and canyon walls of the Crystal Vale are known to house valuable veins of rich thorium, making it a lucrative though hazardous destination for high-skill miners.",["class:Shaman"]="The raw friction between earth and air spirits here serves as a potent reminder of the unbridled chaos of unrestrained elementals across Silithus."},kw={"crystal vale","elementals","highlord demitrian","ravaged twilight camp","silithus","thorium","thunderaan"},rel={"npc:highlord-demitrian","npc:thunderaan","subzone:ravaged-twilight-camp","zone:silithus"},src={"Crystal Vale"}}
E["subzone:hive-ashi"] = {t="subzone",n="Hive'Ashi",z="silithus",s="Hive'Ashi is a sprawling silithid colony dominating the northern sands of Silithus. As one of three major insectoid hives in the region, its creeping tunnels and towering mounds churn with countless hostile workers, defenders, and stingers.",h="Hive'Ashi is a sprawling silithid colony dominating the northern sands of Silithus.",sec={{t="The Northern Mound",b="Situated in northern Silithus, Hive'Ashi serves as a prime hive-complex for the re-emerging silithid swarms. Its chitinous spires carve out a distinct territory among the dunes, sending foraging workers and venomous defenders south and east toward the Swarming Pillar. Anyone seeking to understand the strange, coordinated intelligence stirring within the desert wastes inevitably finds their path leading directly into the dangerous, buzzing tunnels beneath these mounds.",sp=0},{t="A Threat Unearthed",b="Cenarion scouts stationed across Silithus monitor Hive'Ashi closely, commissioning brave combatants to thin its ranks and retrieve reconnaissance reports from deep within the colony. The glyphs and coordinated behavior documented within Ashi suggest that these mindless-looking insects share an eerie, singular will. As their numbers swell, the hive threatens to spill beyond northern Silithus entirely, making the eradication of its brood a top priority for those watching the southern borders.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Hive'Ashi?",a="Hive'Ashi is an active silithid hive-complex located in northern Silithus. It is home to thousands of burrowing insectoid creatures that hollow out the desert sands into interconnected tunnels and mounds.",al={"ashi hive","hive ashi location","what is ashi"}},{q="What kinds of silithid live in Hive'Ashi?",a="The colony is populated by specialized castes of silithid, including Hive'Ashi workers, sandstalkers, venomous stingers, and heavily armored defenders.",al={"ashi mobs","hive ashi creatures","what silithid are here"}},{q="How does Hive'Ashi relate to the Swarming Pillar?",a="The silithid swarming around the nearby Swarming Pillar originate from Hive'Ashi, representing an outward push of the hive's brood across the desert floor.",al={"swarming pillar connection","ashi and swarming pillar"}},{q="Why are Cenarion scouts studying this hive?",a="The Cenarion Circle seeks to understand the rapid resurgence of the silithid and how their hives coordinate. Scouts monitor Ashi to decipher strange glyphs and track how quickly the hive is expanding.",al={"why scout hive ashi","hive ashi scout report"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As the Cenarion Circle watches the corrupted sands of Silithus, druids are called upon to study and suppress the insectoid menace churning out from Hive'Ashi before it engulfs the natural ecosystem.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance operatives moving through Silithus aid in gathering intelligence on Hive'Ashi to ensure these aggressive swarms do not threaten neighboring territories across southern Kalimdor."},kw={"cenarion","hive ashi","hive'ashi","silithid","silithus","swarming pillar"},rel={"zone:silithus","subzone:swarming-pillar"},src={"Hive'Ashi"}}
E["subzone:hive-regal"] = {t="subzone",n="Hive'Regal",z="silithus",s="Hive'Regal is a massive silithid hive burrowed into the southern reaches of Silithus. As one of the three primary insectoid colonies dominating the arid wastes, it teems with aggressive silithid castes that threaten to overrun the surrounding desert.",h="Hive'Regal is a massive silithid hive burrowed into the southern reaches of Silithus.",sec={{t="The Southern Hive",b="Sprawling across southern Silithus, Hive'Regal represents one of the greatest concentrations of silithid activity in Kalimdor. Its towering resin spires and cavernous underground tunnels churn with dangerous insectoid broods, from venomous spitfires and burrowers to predatory slavemakers. The hive acts as a coordinated warren, aggressively defending its perimeter and harvesting organic material from any unfortunate travelers who wander too close to its borders.",sp=0},{t="Subterranean Network",b="Beneath the red sands, Hive'Regal's labyrinthine passages delve deep into the earth. Strange glyphs etched near its entrance and deep inside the tunnels suggest an organized intelligence directing the swarm rather than mere feral instinct. Scholars and scouts studying the silithid threat believe that Hive'Regal, along with its sister hives, functions as part of a larger emergent power stirring beneath the wastes of Silithus.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Hive'Regal located?",a="Hive'Regal is located in the southern region of Silithus, marked by distinct towering insectoid mounds and infested red sands.",al={"hive regal location","where is hive regal","find hive regal"}},{q="What kinds of creatures live in Hive'Regal?",a="The nest is inhabited by various hostile silithid breeds, including burrowers, ambushers, spitfires, and slavemakers that aggressively defend the hive.",al={"hive regal mobs","what is inside hive regal","hive regal enemies"}},{q="Why are researchers interested in Hive'Regal?",a="Scouts and scholars study the hive to decipher strange communicative glyphs found on its walls and to monitor the growing threat of the silithid swarm across southern Kalimdor.",al={"why go to hive regal","hive regal research","hive regal glyphs"}},{q="How does Hive'Regal differ from the other hives in Silithus?",a="Hive'Regal is the southernmost of the three major colonies in Silithus, alongside Hive'Ashi and Hive'Zora. Each colony houses specialized castes of silithid, though all appear to share a unified, insidious purpose.",al={"other hives silithus","three hives","difference between hives"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="The Cenarion Circle closely monitors the spread of Hive'Regal, recognizing the invasive silithid corruption as an existential blight upon the desert ecosystem."},kw={"burrowers","hive","hive'regal","regal","silithid","silithus","slavemakers","spitfires"},rel={"zone:silithus"},src={"Hive'Regal"}}
E["subzone:hive-zora"] = {t="subzone",n="Hive'Zora",z="silithus",s="Hive'Zora is one of the three major silithid colony mounds dominating the arid expanse of Silithus. Located along the western edge of the desert, this teeming subterranean hive crawls with aggressive insectoid castes serving the greater swarm.",h="Hive'Zora is one of the three major silithid colony mounds dominating the arid expanse of Silithus.",sec={{t="The Western Swarm",b="Rising out of the barren sand dunes of western Silithus, Hive'Zora serves as a bustling hub of insectoid activity. Great, porous stone spires and mounds mark the entrances into deep subterranean tunnels dug out by silithid burrowers. Waywatchers and reavers patrol the perimeter relentlessly, while tunneling castes and hive sisters brood within the depths below. For the Cenarion Circle and other scouts keeping watch over the desert, the hive represents a terrifying sign of the insectoid menace steadily reclaiming the ancient frontier.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Hive'Zora?",a="Hive'Zora is an active silithid hive complex situated in western Silithus. It consists of massive insectoid spires on the surface connected to sprawling subterranean tunnels.",al={"zora hive","what is hive zora","hive zora silithus"}},{q="What creatures live in Hive'Zora?",a="The hive is occupied entirely by the silithid swarm. Distinct castes inhabit the mound, including Hive'Zora waywatchers patrolling the outside, heavy reavers defending the ground, tunnelers excavating the earth, and venomous hive sisters.",al={"hive zora mobs","what monsters are in hive zora","who lives in hive zora"}},{q="Why is the Cenarion Circle investigating this hive?",a="Scouts and researchers stationed in Silithus observe Hive'Zora to track the growth and movement of the silithid threat. Envoys study their behaviors, decrypt their glyphs, and thin their expanding numbers before the insect swarm can overwhelm the region.",al={"why scout hive zora","cenarion circle hive zora"}},{q="How does Hive'Zora differ from the other hives in Silithus?",a="Hive'Zora is the westernmost of the three great hives, with Hive'Ashi anchoring the north and Hive'Regal dominating the south. Each hive operates with its own distinct brood, though all share the same predatory drive to expand across the desert.",al={"other hives silithus","difference between hives","hive regal hive ashi"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For the Druids of the Cenarion Circle, Hive'Zora represents a terrifying unnatural surge that disrupts the natural balance of the desert wilds.",["profession:Mining"]="The twisted tunnels and perimeter of silithid colonies like Hive'Zora often expose valuable rich thorium veins and rare ooze-covered mineral deposits."},kw={"cenarion circle","hive sisters","hive zora","hive'zora","reavers","silithid","silithus","waywatchers"},rel={"zone:silithus"},src={"Hive'Zora"}}
E["subzone:ortell-s-hideout"] = {t="subzone",n="Ortell's Hideout",z="silithus",s="Ortell's Hideout is a modest, secluded cave nestled against the mountains in southeastern Silithus. It serves as the refuge of Hermit Ortell, one of the few solitary souls hardy or foolish enough to dwell alone in this barren wasteland.",h="Ortell's Hideout is a modest, secluded cave nestled against the mountains in southeastern Silithus.",sec={{t="A Hermit's Shelter",b="Tucked away in the jagged cliffs of southeastern Silithus, Ortell's Hideout offers sparse sanctuary from the raging sandstorms and prowling silithid swarms that dominate the wastes. The cave is occupied solely by Hermit Ortell, an eccentric recluse who ekes out an existence far from civilization and the fortified garrisons of the Cenarion Hold. Travelers who brave the dangerous journey to this remote corner often seek his peculiar knowledge of the desert and its hazards.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Ortell's Hideout?",a="The hideout is carved into the mountain rock along the southeastern edge of Silithus, far from the central desert roads and nestled deep against the border cliffs.",al={"where is ortell","ortell location","how to find ortell cave"}},{q="Who is Hermit Ortell?",a="Hermit Ortell is a solitary dweller living apart from the Cenarion Circle expedition and the factions of the world. He chooses to reside alone amidst the dangers of Silithus, keeping to his small cave.",al={"who is ortell","hermit ortell lore"}},{q="Is Ortell's Hideout safe from the silithid?",a="While the cave itself is not infested, it lies isolated in a deeply hostile zone teeming with insectoid silithid and Twilight's Hammer cultists. Reaching the hideout requires cutting through perilous terrain.",al={"are there bugs in the cave","is ortell cave safe"}}},kw={"cave","hermit ortell","ortell's hideout","silithus","southeastern silithus"},rel={"zone:silithus","subzone:mountain-den"},src={"Ortell's Hideout"}}
E["subzone:ravaged-twilight-camp"] = {t="subzone",n="Ravaged Twilight Camp",z="silithus",s="Tucked away in the secluded Crystal Vale of northwestern Silithus, the Ravaged Twilight Camp sits ruined among towering mineral formations. It serves as an isolated redoubt for the eccentric hermit Highlord Demitrian, a devotee of the Windseeker.",h="Tucked away in the secluded Crystal Vale of northwestern Silithus, the Ravaged Twilight Camp sits ruined...",sec={{t="A Hermit's Ruin in the Vale",b="While the Twilight's Hammer maintains numerous active outposts across the sands of Silithus, this broken encampment in the Crystal Vale tells a different story. Nestled far from the primary cult fortresses, the camp lies largely ruined and deserted, save for Highlord Demitrian. A servant of Thunderaan, Demitrian lingers amidst the stones, seemingly abandoned by or detached from the wider Twilight hierarchy while brooding over elemental bindings and the lost power of the Windseeker.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Ravaged Twilight Camp?",a="It is a battered, ruined outpost located within the Crystal Vale in northwestern Silithus, notable as the personal dwelling of Highlord Demitrian.",al={"ravaged twilight camp","ruined twilight camp silithus","crystal vale camp"}},{q="Who lives here?",a="The sole notable resident is Highlord Demitrian, a solitary figure deeply tied to elemental lore and the bindings of Prince Thunderaan.",al={"who is at the ravaged twilight camp","highlord demitrian location","camp npc"}},{q="Why is the camp ruined?",a="Cult records mention the site's ruined state, but Demitrian remains amidst the wreckage, isolated from the rest of the Twilight's Hammer operating in Silithus.",al={"why is it ravaged","what destroyed the camp","who attacked the camp"}},{q="Is the Twilight's Hammer hostile here?",a="Unlike the bustling Twilight camps across southern and central Silithus, this camp lacks aggressive cult patrols, leaving Demitrian to brood in peace.",al={"are cultists attacking here","is demitrian hostile"}}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="Any warrior hunting rumors of the legendary blade Thunderfury, Blessed Blade of the Windseeker, will eventually find their path leading straight to Highlord Demitrian in this forsaken camp.",["class:Paladin"]="Those seeking the legendary elemental armaments of antiquity must seek out Demitrian in the Crystal Vale to unravel the vessel of Prince Thunderaan."},kw={"crystal vale","demitrian","highlord demitrian","ravaged twilight camp","silithus","thunderaan","thunderfury","twilight's hammer"},rel={"subzone:crystal-vale","npc:highlord-demitrian","zone:silithus"},src={"Ravaged Twilight Camp"}}
E["subzone:scarab-dais"] = {t="subzone",n="Scarab Dais",z="silithus",s="The Scarab Dais is an ancient raised platform situated northwest of the Scarab Wall in southern Silithus. It holds the legendary Scarab Gong, the ritual instrument tied directly to the magical wards sealing the qiraji empire within Ahn'Qiraj.",h="The Scarab Dais is an ancient raised platform situated northwest of the Scarab Wall in southern Silithus.",sec={{t="The Gong of Ahn'Qiraj",b="Overlooking the shifting sands before the colossal barrier of the Scarab Wall, the Scarab Dais serves as the focal point for the seal placed upon Ahn'Qiraj a millennium ago. Upon this stone dais rests the Scarab Gong, a relic forged during the War of the Shifting Sands. According to ancient night elven history and the bronze dragonflight, striking this gong with the reconstructed Scepter of the Shifting Sands is the only means to shatter the magical barrier and breach the gates. Until that fateful moment arrives, the platform remains an ominous vigil over the sealed insectoid horrors slumbering beyond the wall.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Scarab Dais?",a="The Scarab Dais is a stone ceremonial terrace in southern Silithus, perched just northwest of the Scarab Wall. It was constructed to house the Scarab Gong, which controls the magical wards sealing Ahn'Qiraj.",al={"what is this platform","scarab dais info","gong platform"}},{q="What happens if someone rings the gong on the dais?",a="Legend says that striking the Scarab Gong with the restored Scepter of the Shifting Sands will shatter the wards across the Scarab Wall, unsealing the gates of Ahn'Qiraj and releasing the qiraji armies imprisoned within.",al={"what does the gong do","ring scarab gong","bang a gong"}},{q="Who watches over the Scarab Dais?",a="Agents of the bronze dragonflight, such as the dragon Rhonormu, watch over the dais and the sealed gate, keeping guard against mortals and cultists who would tamper with the barrier prematurely.",al={"who is at the dais","bronze dragons at the dais","rhonormu"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei, the Scarab Dais is a stark reminder of the tragic War of the Shifting Sands a thousand years ago, where night elves and dragonflights paid in blood to seal the qiraji behind the wall."},kw={"ahn'qiraj","rhonormu","scarab dais","scarab gong","scarab wall","shifting sands","silithus"},rel={"subzone:scarab-wall","zone:silithus"},src={"Scarab Dais"}}
E["subzone:scarab-wall"] = {t="subzone",n="Scarab Wall",z="silithus",s="The Scarab Wall is a colossal barricade sealing off the southern border of Silithus from the insectoid empire of Ahn'Qiraj. Conjured at the end of the War of the Shifting Sands, the barrier combines stone and bronze dragonflight sorcery to keep ancient, crawling horrors contained. Today, it stands as an imposing reminder of the terrible cost paid to seal away the silithid menace.",h="The Scarab Wall is a colossal barricade sealing off the southern border of Silithus from the insectoid empire...",sec={{t="Shield Against the Shadow",b="Spanning the desert from east to west, the Scarab Wall was raised a thousand years ago at the conclusion of the catastrophic War of the Shifting Sands. Pushed to the brink of annihilation by the qiraji, the night elf armies and their dragon allies forced the swarms back into their ancient kingdom. To contain them permanently, the kaldorei shaped the desert stone into an immense rampart standing at least a hundred feet tall, while the bronze dragonflight wove a colossal magical barrier above it. Known in Darnassian as Irana'ethil—the 'Shield against the Shadow'—the wall successfully severed the insectoid armies from Kalimdor, though the dread presence locked behind its stone remains palpable.",sp=0},{t="A Sealed Ruin",b="Beyond the sandstone masonry and shimmering draconic wards lies the ruined city of Ahn'Qiraj, a stronghold built around an ancient, malevolent force. While the massive gates remain firmly shut, the recent surge of silithid hives across southern Kalimdor suggests that the barrier's seal may not hold forever. Mortal explorers who approach the wall can hear the muffled scratching of chitinous legs and feel the oppressive shadow that lingers over the entire perimeter.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Scarab Wall?",a="The Scarab Wall is a massive stone and magical barrier at the southern edge of Silithus. It was erected to seal away the ancient insectoid kingdom of Ahn'Qiraj and keep its ravenous swarms trapped within their desert ruins.",al={"scarab wall purpose","what is this wall in silithus","ahn qiraj wall"}},{q="Who built the Scarab Wall?",a="It was created jointly by the night elves and the bronze dragonflight at the culmination of the War of the Shifting Sands. The elves molded the desert rock into a hundred-foot-tall wall, while the dragons projected an immense magical barrier over it.",al={"who made the wall","who created the scarab wall"}},{q="What does Irana'ethil mean?",a="Irana'ethil is the Darnassian name given to the Scarab Wall by the night elves who shaped it. It translates roughly to 'Shield against the Shadow.'",al={"irana'ethil meaning","elven name for scarab wall"}},{q="Can players go past the wall?",a="No. The gates are sealed tight by ancient draconic enchantments, making the ruined kingdom behind it completely inaccessible to travelers.",al={"can you go past scarab wall","how to get past wall in silithus"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, this wall is a sacred monument to the horrific sacrifices made during the War of the Shifting Sands, where an entire generation was lost to halt the swarm.",["class:Druid"]="Druids feel the unnatural suppression of life around the perimeter, where ancient wards struggle to contain a corruptive, subterranean blight."},kw={"ahn'qiraj","bronze dragonflight","irana'ethil","qiraji","scarab wall","silithus","war of the shifting sands"},rel={"zone:silithus","topic:old-god","subzone:valor-s-rest"},src={"Scarab Wall"}}
E["subzone:southwind-village"] = {t="subzone",n="Southwind Village",z="silithus",s="Southwind Village is the haunted ruin of a night elf outpost located in the sands of Silithus. Wiped out by the qiraji during the War of the Shifting Sands, its streets are now bound by the restless spirits of fallen defenders and prowling silithid.",h="Southwind Village is the haunted ruin of a night elf outpost located in the sands of Silithus.",sec={{t="A Tragedy in the Sands",b="Southwind Village once served as a primary night elf stronghold during the ancient War of the Shifting Sands a thousand years ago. When the qiraji legions breached the defensive perimeter, Valstann Staghelm—son of Archdruid Fandral Staghelm—led a detachment to hold the village. The defense ended in utter disaster: the night elven defenders were overwhelmed and slaughtered, and Valstann himself was dragged away into captivity by General Rajaxx. The village was completely ruined, leaving its former buildings fractured under the sun.",sp=0},{t="The Tormented Dead",b="A millennium after its fall, Southwind Village remains an open wound in the desert. The trauma of the assault was so absolute that the spirits of the slain night elf Sentinels and druids could not move on. Driven mad by the horror of their final moments, these restless phantoms—led by the Shade of Ambermoon—endlessly roam the crumbled stone walls, lashing out at any who intrude while predatory silithid swarm the surrounding dunes.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What happened to Southwind Village?",a="Southwind Village was destroyed a thousand years ago during the War of the Shifting Sands. The ravenous qiraji army swarmed the night elven garrison, mercilessly butchering its defenders and flattening the outpost.",al={"why is southwind ruined","southwind lore","what destroyed southwind village"}},{q="Who was Valstann Staghelm?",a="Valstann Staghelm was the beloved son of Archdruid Fandral Staghelm. He led the desperate defense of Southwind Village against the invading insectoids, but his troops were decimated and he was captured by the qiraji commander, General Rajaxx.",al={"valstann staghelm southwind","fandral staghelm son","who defended southwind"}},{q="Why are there night elf ghosts here?",a="The sudden and brutal slaughter of the defenders trapped their souls in the ruins. The spirits of the slain druids and Sentinels are caught in an eternal loop of their final, terrifying battle, overseen by the lingering Shade of Ambermoon.",al={"southwind spirits","why are there ghosts in southwind","shade of ambermoon"}},{q="Are the bugs related to what destroyed the village?",a="Yes. The silithid swarming around the ruins are part of the broader insectoid scourge tied to the qiraji, the very force that invaded Silithus and destroyed the outpost centuries ago.",al={"silithid southwind","are bugs connected to southwind"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, Southwind Village represents one of the most agonizing defeats in their history, and the tortured specters wandering its broken masonry are fellow kaldorei awaiting peace.",["class:Druid"]="The ruined grove-like structures and tormented spirits of ancient druids lingering in Southwind serve as a grim reminder of nature's loss against the insectoid hordes."},kw={"fandral staghelm","qiraji","rajaxx","shade of ambermoon","silithus","southwind village","valstann staghelm","war of the shifting sands"},rel={"zone:silithus","npc:fandral-staghelm","topic:night-elf","topic:sentinels","topic:druid"},src={"Southwind Village"}}
E["subzone:staghelm-point"] = {t="subzone",n="Staghelm Point",z="silithus",s="Staghelm Point is an ancient night elven watchtower perched atop a craggy peak in northeastern Silithus. Overlooking the encroaching dunes and the nearby caverns of Twilight's Run, the tower stands as a vigil against the ancient threats haunting the desert.",h="Staghelm Point is an ancient night elven watchtower perched atop a craggy peak in northeastern Silithus.",sec={{t="A Silent Watch Above the Sands",b="Rising high above the arid flats of northeastern Silithus, Staghelm Point is crowned by a solitary night elf tower. The outpost serves as a lonely sentinel, keeping watch over the wasteland and the shadowed cultists lurking in nearby caves like Twilight's Run. Watched over by Ralo'shan the Eternal Watcher and accompanied by a bronze drake circling overhead, the tower bears the proud and tragic name of the Staghelm lineage—a reminder of the immense sacrifices made by the Kaldorei during the ancient War of the Shifting Sands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is this outpost named Staghelm Point?",a="The tower bears the name of the Staghelm family, honoring either Archdruid Fandral Staghelm—who commanded the night elven forces in the ancient War of the Shifting Sands—or his son Valstann, who was brutally slain by the silithid during that conflict.",al={"staghelm point name","why is it called staghelm point","who is it named after"}},{q="Who lives at Staghelm Point?",a="The solitary tower is guarded by Ralo'shan the Eternal Watcher, while a majestic bronze drake from the Brood of Nozdormu keeps a perpetual patrol in the skies above.",al={"who is at staghelm point","staghelm point npcs","raloshan"}},{q="What threats lie nearby?",a="Down the path winding away from the peak lies Twilight's Run, a cavern and surrounding camp crawling with fanatical members of the Twilight's Hammer cult.",al={"staghelm point danger","nearby enemies","twilights run"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Staghelm Point evokes the solemn history of the War of the Shifting Sands, standing as a stark reminder of the Kaldorei's heavy sacrifices in holding back the horrors beneath Silithus.",["class:Druid"]="The tower honors the lineage of Archdruid Fandral Staghelm, offering a contemplative vantage over the corrupted, arid wilderness that defies the balance of nature."},kw={"bronze drake","fandral staghelm","ralo'shan","silithus","staghelm point","twilight's run","valstann staghelm","watchtower"},rel={"zone:silithus","npc:fandral-staghelm","subzone:twilight-s-run","topic:cenarion-circle","topic:night-elf","topic:druid"},src={"Staghelm Point"}}
E["subzone:swarming-pillar"] = {t="subzone",n="Swarming Pillar",z="silithus",s="The Swarming Pillar is a towering rock formation in the heart of Silithus, thoroughly infested and reshaped by the silithid. Situated just south of Cenarion Hold, the spire takes its name from the relentless clouds of winged insectoids buzzing around its peaks and subterranean entrances.",h="The Swarming Pillar is a towering rock formation in the heart of Silithus, thoroughly infested and reshaped...",sec={{t="A Spire of Chitin and Sand",b="Rising abruptly from the shifting dunes of central Silithus, the Swarming Pillar serves as a grim monument to the unchecked expansion of the silithid. What began as a natural rock formation has been carved and encrusted with the resinous secretions and burrows of the insectoid swarm. Just south of Cenarion Hold, it constantly churns out broods of winged workers and soldiers, whose dark clouds fill the dry desert air and warn travelers to keep their distance.",sp=0},{t="Heart of the Hive",b="Though massive and intimidating on the surface, the Swarming Pillar is merely the outward protrusion of a vast underground network. Beneath its stony exterior lie deep tunnels and cavernous breeding chambers that anchor one of the largest hives in the region. The Cenarion Circle views the spire with immense concern, as its active broods directly threaten druidic operations and hint at the terrifying coordination behind the insectoid menace.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Swarming Pillar?",a="The Swarming Pillar is a massive rock formation in central Silithus that has been overtaken and turned into an active silithid hive. It is characterized by the endless swarm of flying insectoids circling its peak.",al={"swarming pillar","what is this pillar","silithid spire silithus"}},{q="Where is the Swarming Pillar located?",a="You can find it in the center of the desert, just a short distance directly south of Cenarion Hold.",al={"where is swarming pillar","swarming pillar location"}},{q="Why are there so many bugs flying around it?",a="The rock formation houses one of the primary hives in Silithus, serving as a massive nursery and transit point for winged silithid that patrol the surrounding desert sands.",al={"why swarming","flying bugs silithus pillar","flying silithid"}},{q="Is the Swarming Pillar connected to the hives beneath the sand?",a="Yes. The visible spire is just the topmost projection of an extensive subterranean colony carved deep into the bedrock and sands beneath Silithus.",al={"hive tunnels","underground silithid pillar"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Standing so close to Cenarion Hold, the hive at the Swarming Pillar is an immediate affront to the natural order and an ongoing danger to the Cenarion Circle's watch."},kw={"cenarion hold","hive","insects","silithid","silithus","spire","swarming pillar"},rel={"zone:silithus","subzone:cenarion-hold"},src={"Swarming Pillar"}}
E["subzone:twilight-base-camp"] = {t="subzone",n="Twilight Base Camp",z="silithus",s="The Twilight Base Camp is a fortified outpost of the Twilight's Hammer cult situated in the arid wastes of Silithus. It serves as an active ritual site where cultists convene to commune with elemental powers and orchestrate their apocalyptic agenda. The camp is characterized by strange wind stones and heavily armed cult zealots.",h="The Twilight Base Camp is a fortified outpost of the Twilight's Hammer cult situated in the arid wastes of...",sec={{t="A Bastion of Doom",b="Perched among the desolate sands of Silithus, the Twilight Base Camp is one of several enclaves established by the Twilight's Hammer cult. The outpost brims with zealots, geomancers, and stonecallers dedicated to summoning devastating elemental forces. Surrounded by jagged ritual stones, the camp acts as a staging ground where leaders like Twilight Keeper Havunth and Twilight Lord Everun direct efforts to hasten Azeroth's end, standing in open defiance of the Cenarion Hold forces attempting to restore balance to the region.",sp=0},{t="The Wind Stones",b="Scattered throughout the outpost are mysterious monuments known as wind stones, ranging in power from lesser conduits to greater monoliths. Through cryptic incantations and cult regalia, the Twilight's Hammer uses these focal points to pull chaotic elemental spirits directly into the physical realm. Disrupting these rituals remains a top priority for travelers and scouts hoping to prevent the cult's influence from spreading across Kalimdor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Twilight Base Camp?",a="It is an armed outpost established by the apocalyptic Twilight's Hammer cult in the deserts of Silithus, used to conduct dark rituals and summon powerful elemental entities.",al={"twilight camp silithus","what is twilight base camp","silithus cultist camp"}},{q="Who controls this camp?",a="The outpost is manned by zealots of the Twilight's Hammer under the direction of overseers such as Twilight Keeper Havunth and the rare leader Twilight Lord Everun.",al={"who leads twilight base camp","twilight base camp leader","who is in charge"}},{q="What are the strange stones in the camp?",a="The structures are wind stones—mystical focal conduits varying in size that cultists use to pierce planar barriers and bind elemental creatures into their service.",al={"wind stones","lesser wind stone","greater wind stone silithus"}},{q="Why are the Twilight's Hammer in Silithus?",a="The cult is drawn to the ancient, chaotic energies lingering beneath the sands of Silithus, seeking to awaken dark powers and summon elementals to bring about the destruction of the world.",al={"why twilight hammer silithus","twilight cult silithus goal"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="The blatant perversion and subjugation of elemental spirits at the camp's wind stones is an affront to any shaman dedicated to maintaining spiritual harmony.",["class:Paladin"]="The dark, apocalyptic rituals conducted by the cultists represent a direct threat to peace, calling for the righteous judgment of the Holy Light."},kw={"silithus","twilight avenger","twilight base camp","twilight geolord","twilight keeper havunth","twilight lord everun","twilight's hammer","wind stones"},rel={"zone:silithus","topic:twilight-s-hammer","topic:light"},src={"Twilight Base Camp"}}
E["subzone:twilight-outpost"] = {t="subzone",n="Twilight Outpost",z="silithus",s="The Twilight Outpost is a fortified encampment of the Twilight's Hammer cult nestled in the southwestern sands of Silithus. Located just northwest of the ancient Scarab Wall, it serves as a staging ground where cultists conduct dark rituals to commune with and summon elemental horrors.",h="The Twilight Outpost is a fortified encampment of the Twilight's Hammer cult nestled in the southwestern...",sec={{t="A Bastion of Whispers",b="Tucked away in the southwestern reaches of Silithus, the Twilight Outpost serves as one of several major cultist strongholds dotting the desert wastes. Positioned in the shadow of the colossal Scarab Wall and west of the Bronzebeard Encampment, the outpost teems with fanatical Twilight Avengers, Geolords, and Stonecallers. Under the command of leaders like Twilight Keeper Exeter and the rare Twilight Lord Everun, these zealots toil tirelessly in service of their maddening apocalyptic masters.",sp=0},{t="The Wind Stones",b="Scattered throughout the encampment are mysterious Wind Stones, varying in size from Lesser to Greater conduits. Through the use of enchanted cultist regalia and foul incantations, the cult utilizes these monoliths to tear into the elemental planes, dragging forth Abyssal commanders and elemental lords. For adventurers brave enough to infiltrate their ranks, disrupting these summonings remains one of the primary means to strike back against the cult's influence in the desert.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Twilight Outpost located?",a="The Twilight Outpost is situated in the far southwestern corner of Silithus. It sits northwest of the ancient Scarab Wall and directly west of the dwarven Bronzebeard Encampment.",al={"twilight outpost location","where is twilight outpost","find twilight outpost"}},{q="Who occupies the Twilight Outpost?",a="The encampment is occupied by the Twilight's Hammer cult. Its ranks include various mortal zealots such as Twilight Avengers, Geolords, Stonecallers, and Twilight Masters, overseen by leaders such as Twilight Keeper Exeter and Twilight Lord Everun.",al={"who is at twilight outpost","twilight outpost enemies","cultists in silithus"}},{q="What are the Wind Stones found in the camp?",a="The Wind Stones—ranging from Lesser to Greater—are mystical foci used by the cult to breach the elemental planes. Cultists channel dark energies through these stones to summon potent elemental lords and Abyssal commanders into Azeroth.",al={"what are wind stones","greater wind stone silithus","lesser wind stone silithus"}},{q="Why is the Twilight's Hammer gathered near the Scarab Wall?",a="The cult is drawn to the potent and ancient dark energies slumbering beneath Silithus. Establishing encampments near the Scarab Wall allows them to perform elemental summonings and harness the chaotic forces stirring beyond the sealed gates.",al={"why are cultists in silithus","twilight hammer purpose silithus"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="The Twilight's Hammer corrupts and commands elemental spirits through their Wind Stones, defying the natural balance of the elements that shamans strive to preserve.",["class:Paladin"]="The nihilistic zealotry of the Twilight's Hammer stands as an affront to the Light, demanding holy wrath to cleanse their foul summonings from the desert."},kw={"bronzebeard encampment","scarab wall","silithus","twilight keeper exeter","twilight lord everun","twilight outpost","twilight's hammer","wind stone"},rel={"zone:silithus","topic:twilight-s-hammer","subzone:scarab-wall","subzone:bronzebeard-encampment","topic:light"},src={"Twilight Outpost"}}
E["subzone:twilight-post"] = {t="subzone",n="Twilight Post",z="silithus",s="Twilight Post is a fortified encampment established by the Twilight's Hammer cult in northwestern Silithus. Situated far west of Cenarion Hold and northwest of the Twilight Base Camp, it serves as a critical site for the cultists' elemental summoning rituals. Adventurers venturing here face zealous cultists and the wind stones they use to contact otherworldly forces.",h="Twilight Post is a fortified encampment established by the Twilight's Hammer cult in northwestern Silithus.",sec={{t="A Bastion of Elemental Zealotry",b="Tucked away in the desert sands of northwestern Silithus, Twilight Post serves as an outpost for the Twilight's Hammer cult. The camp is populated by heavily armed defenders and ritualists, including Twilight Avengers, Geolords, and Stonecallers under the leadership of Twilight Keeper Mayna and the rare fanatic Twilight Lord Everun. Like other encampments scattered across the wastes, the post revolves around ancient summoning conduits—Lesser, regular, and Greater Wind Stones. Through dark rites and elemental communion, the cultists utilize these stones to entreat and bind elemental horrors from the realms beyond, threatening the fragile peace maintained by the Cenarion Circle in the region.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Twilight Post located?",a="Twilight Post is located in the far northwestern reaches of Silithus, situated well to the west of Cenarion Hold and to the northwest of the larger Twilight Base Camp.",al={"twilight post location","where is twilight post","twilight post silithus map"}},{q="Who occupies the Twilight Post?",a="The post is held by the Twilight's Hammer cult. Notable figures stationed here include Twilight Keeper Mayna and Twilight Lord Everun, protected by ranks of Twilight Avengers, Geolords, and Stonecallers.",al={"who is at twilight post","twilight post mobs","enemies at twilight post"}},{q="What are the wind stones found in the camp?",a="The wind stones—ranging from Lesser Wind Stones to regular and Greater Wind Stones—are arcane conduits used by the Twilight's Hammer to summon and bind elemental creatures to their service.",al={"what are wind stones","wind stones silithus","lesser wind stone twilight post"}},{q="Why is the Twilight's Hammer operating in Silithus?",a="The Twilight's Hammer has flocked to the desert wastes of Silithus to awaken and commune with ancient, dark powers slumbering beneath the sands, bolstering their ranks through elemental summonings.",al={"why are cultists in silithus","twilight hammer silithus goal"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="The Twilight's Hammer perverts the sacred communion of the elements, forcefully summoning and binding spirits through the wind stones found at outposts like this one.",["class:Druid"]="The Cenarion Circle watches the rise of the cult's outposts closely, as the cultists' dark elemental rituals threaten to further degrade the fragile, scarred balance of Silithus."},kw={"geolord","silithus","stonecaller","twilight keeper mayna","twilight lord everun","twilight post","twilight's hammer","wind stone"},rel={"zone:silithus","subzone:twilight-base-camp","subzone:cenarion-hold"},src={"Twilight Post"}}
E["subzone:twilight-s-run"] = {t="subzone",n="Twilight's Run",z="silithus",s="Twilight's Run is a secluded subterranean cavern carved into the northern mountains of Silithus beneath Staghelm Point. Occupied by the fanatical Twilight's Hammer cult, it serves as a secluded sanctuary and ritual redoubt away from the harsh desert winds.",h="Twilight's Run is a secluded subterranean cavern carved into the northern mountains of Silithus beneath...",sec={{t="A Subterranean Redoubt",b="Tucked away in the northern cliffside below Staghelm Point, Twilight's Run provides the Twilight's Hammer cultists with a natural bastion amidst the windswept hazards of Silithus. Rather than weathering the dust storms or contending directly with roaming silithid hives across the surface dunes, cultists retreat into these shadowy tunnels to commune with dark forces, guard ritual materials, and marshal their forces. Under the direction of overseers such as Vyral the Vile, cult members within the cave maintain a vigilant, hostile presence, ready to strike down any curious travelers or scouts who draw too close to their subterranean encampment.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Twilight's Run located?",a="Twilight's Run is a cave situated in the northern mountains of Silithus, right at the rocky base beneath Staghelm Point.",al={"where is twilights run","twilights run location","how to find twilights run"}},{q="Who occupies Twilight's Run?",a="The cavern is controlled entirely by members of the Twilight's Hammer, including figures such as Vyral the Vile, Twilight Overlords, and Twilight Flamereavers.",al={"who is inside twilights run","twilights run mobs","who lives in twilights run"}},{q="What is the cult doing inside the cavern?",a="The cult uses the cave as a sheltered redoubt and operational outpost in Silithus, keeping out of the desert elements while furthering their apocalyptic work.",al={"twilight cult purpose silithus cave","why are cultists in twilights run"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="The cloistered depths of Twilight's Run harbor zealous nihilists whose servitude to dark powers stands as an affront to the holy tenets of the Light."},kw={"silithus","staghelm point","twilight cult","twilight's hammer","twilight's run","twilights run","vyral the vile"},rel={"zone:silithus","topic:twilight-s-hammer","subzone:staghelm-point","topic:light"},src={"Twilight's Run"}}
E["subzone:valor-s-rest"] = {t="subzone",n="Valor's Rest",z="silithus",s="Valor's Rest is a small outpost and cemetery perched at the eastern threshold of Silithus. Guarded by members of the Cenarion Circle, it is the first point of shelter seen by travelers emerging from Un'Goro Crater into the windswept wastes.",h="Valor's Rest is a small outpost and cemetery perched at the eastern threshold of Silithus.",sec={{t="Gateway to the Dunes",b="Perched on the eastern border of Silithus along the ramp leading down from Un'Goro Crater, Valor's Rest serves as the threshold into this desolate frontier. Maintained as a neutral staging ground by the Cenarion Circle, the camp hosts members of both the Alliance and the Horde who dare to brave the arid wastes. Its prominent graveyard stands as a somber reminder of the danger lurking throughout the desert, where insectoid horrors and ancient threats test even the hardiest expeditions.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Valor's Rest located?",a="Valor's Rest is situated at the eastern entrance of Silithus. It is the very first settlement encountered when following the path ascending from the northwestern corner of Un'Goro Crater into the desert.",al={"valors rest location","how to find valors rest","where is valors rest"}},{q="Who controls Valor's Rest?",a="The outpost is maintained by the Cenarion Circle. As neutral caretakers studying and guarding the region, they allow both Alliance and Horde travelers to utilize the camp.",al={"who runs valors rest","valors rest faction","cenarion circle camp silithus"}},{q="What is the notable feature of this camp?",a="The most prominent feature of Valor's Rest is its graveyard, marking the graves of those claimed by the unforgiving desert and its encroaching insectoid inhabitants.",al={"valors rest graveyard","what is at valors rest"}},{q="Is Valor's Rest safe from the surrounding wildlife?",a="While it functions as an outpost, the immediate area around the camp suffers from familiar insect infestations, serving as an early forewarning of the swarm lurking deeper within Silithus.",al={"valors rest safe","is valors rest under attack"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As an outpost maintained by the Cenarion Circle, Valor's Rest represents your order's vigilant vigil over the sinister stirrings in the southern desert.",["faction:Alliance"]="Though small and shared with the Horde under Cenarion neutrality, Valor's Rest offers a welcome first refuge upon emerging from the wilds of Un'Goro."},kw={"camp","cenarion circle","graveyard","silithus","un'goro crater","valor's rest"},rel={"zone:silithus","zone:ungoro","topic:cenarion-circle","topic:alliance","topic:horde"},src={"Valor's Rest"}}
E["zone:silithus"] = {t="zone",n="Silithus",z="silithus",s="Silithus is a desolate, wind-scoured desert located in the far southwestern corner of Kalimdor. Beneath its arid sands lie vast colonies of insectoid silithid and the ancient ruins of Ahn'Qiraj, sealed millennia ago behind the formidable Scarab Wall. Today, the druids of the Cenarion Circle maintain an embattled vigil against creeping swarms, doomsday cultists, and mysterious crystalline anomalies.",h="Silithus is a desolate, wind-scoured desert located in the far southwestern corner of Kalimdor.",sec={{t="The Desert Frontier",b="Reaching Silithus requires navigating through the primeval jungle of Un'Goro Crater and ascending a wide, rocky pass nestled in its northwestern corner. The transition is stark: lush primordial growth vanishes into a vast expanse of shifting dunes, jagged stone, and unnatural towering hives. Water is virtually nonexistent, and the winds carry the hum of insect wings and the whispering sands. The Cenarion Circle maintains Cenarion Hold near the center of the desert, serving as the sole bastion of civilization and shelter for travelers, researchers, and warriors braving the hostile wastes.",sp=0},{t="Echoes of the Shifting Sands",b="Thousands of years ago, this arid expanse served as the battlefield for the War of the Shifting Sands. An allied army of night elves and great dragonflights fought desperately to drive back the Qiraji, an insidious insectoid empire spawned from the ancient Aqiri civilization. When total victory proved impossible, the defenders sealed the swarms within their stronghold using the Scarab Wall and the enchanted Scarab Dais. While the monumental gates held, subterranean tunnels allowed the beast-like silithids to burrow out, establishing sprawling colonies such as Hive'Ashi, Hive'Zora, and Hive'Regal throughout the sands.",sp=0},{t="A Converging Storm",b="Recent years have seen tension build to a breaking point across the dunes. The apocalyptic Twilight's Hammer cult has entrenched itself across several fortified outposts, summoning elemental terrors and venerating the dark power slumbering beneath Ahn'Qiraj. Meanwhile, the bronze dragonflight has unexpectedly broken millennia of silence, returning to observe the desert alongside veteran Alliance and Horde detachments. Adding fuel to the conflict, deposits of a strange red powder known as silithyst have emerged from the earth, driving the two factions into open skirmishes for control of the mysterious resource.",sp=0}},faq={{q="How do I get to Silithus on foot?",a="Travel to the northwestern corner of Un'Goro Crater. Near the serpentine river bend, between two prominent natural stone pillars, an inclined dirt roadway leads up through the mountainous crater wall directly into the Silithus desert.",al={"silithus entrance","how to get to silithus","silithus path"}},{q="What is the Scarab Wall?",a="The Scarab Wall is a massive, enchanted barrier in the south of Silithus. It was erected thousands of years ago by the night elves and the dragonflights during the War of the Shifting Sands to imprison the malevolent Qiraji empire within Ahn'Qiraj.",al={"ahn'qiraj gate","scarab wall","the big wall in silithus"}},{q="Who runs Cenarion Hold?",a="Cenarion Hold is an outpost established and run by the Cenarion Circle. Its druids and allied guardians observe the encroaching silithid swarms, investigate ancient ruins, and welcome neutral travelers of both the Alliance and Horde.",al={"who is in cenarion hold","cenarion hold faction","cenarion hold friendly"}},{q="What are the giant insect mounds across the zone?",a="They are the major subterranean hives of the silithids: Hive'Ashi, Hive'Zora, and Hive'Regal. Each hive is a sprawling network of tunnels housing distinct castes of insectoid creatures serving the wills locked behind Ahn'Qiraj.",al={"silithus hives","bug hives silithus","hive ashi hive zora"}},{q="What is silithyst and why are people fighting over it?",a="Silithyst is a volatile, glowing crystalline substance uncovered in geysers across the desert. Both the Alliance and the Horde seek to extract it for study and war materiel, resulting in skirmishes between soldiers carrying dust back to their respective faction encampments.",al={"silithyst dust","silithus pvp","red sand silithus"}},{q="What is the Twilight's Hammer doing here?",a="The Twilight's Hammer cult maintains several fortified bases in Silithus, including the Twilight Base Camp and Twilight Post. They conduct foul rituals to summon elementals and worship the ancient, malevolent entities entombed behind the Scarab Wall.",al={"twilight cultists silithus","twilight outpost silithus","why is twilight's hammer in silithus"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As the heart of Cenarion Circle operations in southern Kalimdor, Silithus calls upon druids to stem the corruption of the land and confront the unnatural broods threatening nature's balance.",["profession:Mining"]="The arid rocks and insect tunnels of Silithus host some of the richest Thorium deposits in the world, including rare ooze-covered veins hidden within the silithid hives.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Despite the harsh desert terrain, rare botanical wonders flourish here, including Mountain Silversage, Dreamfoil, Sungrass, and the exceptionally prized Black Lotus.",["race:NightElf"]="Silithus is the grim resting ground where your ancestors bled during the War of the Shifting Sands, sacrificing thousands to seal the gates of Ahn'Qiraj.",["faction:Alliance"]="The Alliance maintains a forward military presence at the Ironforge Brigade Outpost to harvest silithyst and search for missing heroes such as Brann Bronzebeard.",["faction:Horde"]="The Horde holds an outpost through the Orgrimmar Legion Camp, deploying veterans to gather silithyst resources and contain the encroaching swarms before they reach the Barrens."},kw={"ahn'qiraj","cenarion hold","hive'ashi","hive'regal","hive'zora","scarab dais","scarab wall","silithid","silithus","silithyst","twilight's hammer"},rel={"subzone:cenarion-hold","subzone:scarab-wall","subzone:scarab-dais","zone:ungoro","subzone:hive-ashi","subzone:hive-zora","subzone:hive-regal","topic:cenarion-circle"},src={"Silithus (Classic)","Silithus"}}
